Issue: 

User reports system is slow, unresponsive at times, and applications take an extended period to load.

Environment:

Windows 10/11 workstation
Standard office configuration

Troubleshooting Steps Taken:

Interviewed user to determine symptoms and frequency of issue
Reviewed system resource usage via Task Manager
Identified high memory and/or CPU utilization by active processes
Checked Startup applications for potential performance impact
Evaluated system resource constraints (RAM and overall system performance profile)
Assessed potential need for hardware upgrade based on system limitations

Root Cause (Potential):
System performance degradation likely caused by high resource utilization from background applications and/or hardware limitations (insufficient RAM or CPU capacity).

Resolution:

Identified and reviewed high-impact processes
Disabled non-essential startup applications where appropriate
Recommended hardware upgrade evaluation if performance issues persist

Tools Used:

Task Manager
System Performance Monitoring Tools
Windows system utilities
